  "heading": "\\complex.derivative:of{f}:at{z0}",
  "heading_latex": "\\textrm{complex derivative of }f\\textrm{ at }z_0\\quad\\htmlClass{mlg-title-written}{f'(z_0)}",
  "body_text": null,
  "page": null,
  "source": "[\\complex.derivative:of{f}:at{z0}]\nDefines: d is \\complex\nwhen:\n. z0 is \\\\anything\n. f is \\\\anything\nexpresses:\n. forAll: eps is \\real\n  where: eps \\:real.greater?:/ \\real.zero\n  then:\n  . exists: delta is \\real\n    suchThat:\n    . delta \\:real.greater?:/ \\real.zero\n    . forAll: h is \\complex\n      where:\n      . h != \\complex.zero\n      . \\complex.modulus(h) \\:real.less?:/ delta\n      then: \\complex.modulus(((f(z0 \\.complex.+./ h) \\.complex.-./ f(z0)) \\.complex.div./ h) \\.complex.-./ d) \\:real.less?:/ eps\nDocumented:\n. called: \"complex derivative of $f?$ at $z0?$\"\n. written: \"f?'(z0?)\"\n. description: \"The complex derivative\n                $f'(z_0) = \\lim_{h \\to 0} \\frac{f(z_0 + h) - f(z_0)}{h}$.\"\nId: \"7e3019a7-07f3-462e-bd30-6047f158b5de\"",
